NAME
       opendir, readdir, closedir - read a directory

SYNOPSIS
       #include <dirent.h>

       DIR           *opendir(const char *path);
       struct dirent *readdir(DIR *d);
       int            closedir(DIR *d);

DESCRIPTION
       Iterates over a directory. Each entry carries d_name and d_type;
       d_type says whether the entry is a directory without a separate
       stat call, which is worth using when listing large trees.

       The returned entry is overwritten by the next readdir, so copy
       anything you need to keep.

RETURN VALUE
       readdir returns NULL at the end of the directory and on error.

SEE ALSO
       getdents(2), stat(2), fnmatch(3)
